1
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:29,410
[Live Forever]

2
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:32,940
[Episode 2]

3
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:35,970
[2026]

4
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:36,470
For ordinary people,

5
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,920
marriage may be

6
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:40,150
the most sincere and intimate relationship

7
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:42,840
they will ever have.

8
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:44,940
Loyalty

9
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:47,090
is the promise of exclusivity

10
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:49,090
that binds two people in a marriage.

11
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,970
But for some people,

12
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:56,460
marriage is just a seasoning
for a long life,

13
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:58,730
or

14
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:01,420
a badge they wear in a game.

15
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,380
Honey.

16
00:01:10,539 --> 00:01:13,420
Can you cut it a little smaller next time?

17
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:15,420
I can't even chew it.

18
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:16,789
No problem.

19
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,910
You came out to see me wearing a ring.

20
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,890
Aren't you afraid she'll find out?

21
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:28,810
What's there to be afraid of?

22
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:30,860
Afraid she'll be jealous.

23
00:01:33,229 --> 00:01:34,390
Then

24
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:35,979
wouldn't this

25
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,860
just make her even more jealous?

26
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:43,479
You're such a tease.

27
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:48,620
Then if she and I fell
into the water together,

28
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:50,539
who would you save first?

29
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:54,340
That sounds like a classic
wife-and-mother-in-law question.

30
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:58,530
Of course I'd save you.

31
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,730
She won't die anyway.

32
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,060
How does it taste?

33
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,220
I prepared it especially for you.

34
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,220
It's from the Alba region.

35
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:18,079
But there was too much rain this year,

36
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:20,940
so the aroma is a bit lighter
than in previous years.

37
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:22,940
It's handled okay.

38
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,890
The finish lingers longer.

39
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:26,850
Miss Song,

40
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,900
these are my family heirlooms.

41
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:30,090
Pick whatever

42
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:31,090
you like.

43
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:33,770
You don't need to consider
the price at all.

44
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:48,020
To be honest,

45
00:02:48,570 --> 00:02:50,570
they are all tacky.

46
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:54,740
Where is the auction invitation
you promised me?

47
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:55,670
What do you mean?

48
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:57,280
It's right here.

49
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:00,410
He's no good.

50
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:01,740
I'm in a hurry to meet someone else.

51
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,670
I won't be home for dinner tonight.

52
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,540
See you next time, Miss Lin.

53
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,240
Ning Changyue,

54
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:12,940
why is she here?

55
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:16,010
Is it fun
to bring your ex-wife on a date?

56
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:17,620
Wait,

57
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,500
you two still live together?

58
00:03:21,829 --> 00:03:23,360
I've already paid the bill.

59
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:24,690
Ning Changyue.

60
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:25,940
Love you, baby.

61
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:26,850
Ning Changyue!

62
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,130
Wait!

63
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:35,470
Give me a ride.

64
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,620
Sure.

65
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:39,270
Miss Lin.

66
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:45,920
Miss Song.

67
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:48,850
Hey.

68
00:03:49,170 --> 00:03:50,450
Why did I see Miss Song go over there?

69
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:51,650
Call her Auntie Song.

70
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:55,760
You didn't get caught by her
while out on a date, did you?

71
00:03:56,550 --> 00:03:57,329
What do you mean?

72
00:03:57,329 --> 00:03:58,860
Isn't she here on a date too?

73
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:00,180
For young people,

74
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,280
this is a healthy relationship.

75
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:06,550
[Healthy Relationship]

76
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:06,300
A healthy relationship?

77
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:11,810
[2000]

78
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:13,500
Song Yiqiu,

79
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:14,900
let's

80
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,000
be together again.

81
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:19,370
We began this journey
to immortality together,

82
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:19,860
so let's

83
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:22,780
bring it to an end together.

84
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:30,730
Really nice.

85
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:32,010
Italian decoration.

86
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,180
Very good.

87
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,540
Put that Ming Dynasty vase

88
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:37,010
on the third shelf of the display cabinet.

89
00:04:37,010 --> 00:04:38,930
The painting is crooked.
A little to the left.

90
00:04:38,930 --> 00:04:39,520
Forget it.

91
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,520
I'll do it myself.

92
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:41,690
Ning Changyue.

93
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:43,570
You can move in,

94
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:45,690
but we need to set some ground rules.

95
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:46,540
First,

96
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,620
don't touch my things.

97
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:49,860
Second,

98
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:51,210
when I'm not talking to you,

99
00:04:51,210 --> 00:04:52,450
don't talk to me.

100
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,400
Third,

101
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,800
if I'm upset,

102
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:56,860
don't show up in front of me.

103
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,340
The first two are fine.

104
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:00,370
As for the third,

105
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,800
how am I supposed to know
when you're upset?

106
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,290
This Ming Dynasty piece is still the best.

107
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:09,060
So you mean

108
00:05:09,970 --> 00:05:11,460
you disagree?

109
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:13,510
Be careful!

110
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,560
What are you doing?

111
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:18,620
After all, if these

112
00:05:18,890 --> 00:05:20,420
Ming Dynasty vases break,

113
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,060
they're just shards of pottery.

114
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:22,580
Okay, okay.

115
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,510
Whatever you say.

116
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:24,240
Give it to me.

117
00:05:33,010 --> 00:05:34,320
My stocks.

118
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:37,340
My stocks, my stocks.

119
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:39,860
The weather is so nice today.

120
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:43,250
We must have a perfect Christmas.

121
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:54,450
Ning Changyue.

122
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,460
What's wrong?

123
00:05:59,659 --> 00:06:01,060
My little Qiuqiu.

124
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:06,170
Merry Christmas.

125
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,100
Wait a minute.

126
00:06:22,210 --> 00:06:23,130
Are you selling it or not?

127
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:24,100
Let me think about it.

128
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:26,210
Why are you so indecisive?

129
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:27,130
What do you know?

130
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,010
This is the first edition.

131
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:29,500
Song Yiqiu, be the judge.

132
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:35,550
You little brat.

133
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,390
Take it away.

134
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,170
Much quieter now.

135
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,520
No, I don't want it.

136
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:55,380
[2026]

137
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:57,690
I've known you for so many years.

138
00:06:58,570 --> 00:07:00,370
When have you ever been healthy?

139
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:10,450
Handle with care.

140
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:11,980
That's Ming Dynasty rosewood.

141
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:12,980
If it breaks,

142
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,430
even selling you wouldn't cover the cost.

143
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,540
These treasures of yours

144
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,180
are worth more than me.

145
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:22,810
Take your time.

146
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:23,740
Enjoy your meal.

147
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,420
I'm off work!

148
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:29,660
You have quite the style now.

149
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:31,110
It's the 21st century,

150
00:07:31,130 --> 00:07:32,930
and you still have an entourage.

151
00:07:33,010 --> 00:07:34,300
They're called employees now,

152
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:35,300
old lady.

153
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:37,180
We offer full social insurance
and housing provident fund benefits,

154
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:39,300
legal employment,
and a formal employment contract.

155
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,250
You've been living

156
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:42,580
too comfortably these past twenty years.

157
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:45,610
Drinking tea, appraising antiques,
and ordering people around.

158
00:07:45,610 --> 00:07:46,930
Have you forgotten

159
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:49,100
why we've been pretending
to live in harmony

160
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:50,060
under this roof?

161
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:51,790
Of course I haven't forgotten.

162
00:07:52,159 --> 00:07:53,480
I'm not like some people

163
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,210
who use blind dates as an excuse

164
00:07:55,450 --> 00:07:56,330
to trick those

165
00:07:56,330 --> 00:07:58,180
rich and resourceful collectors

166
00:07:58,180 --> 00:07:59,480
into finding the osmanthus tree.

167
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,500
I'll give her credit
for coming up with that one.

168
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,660
At least I'm genuinely trying to find it.

169
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:04,570
What about you?

170
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,790
Miss Lin, Miss Wang and Miss Liu.

171
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:08,980
Are you looking for a painting

172
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:10,360
or holding a beauty pageant?

173
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,000
At least I'm efficient.

174
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,260
Unlike some people

175
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:14,620
who've been going on blind dates for ages

176
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:17,500
and still end up with
nothing but vulgar types.

177
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:19,980
Even a vulgar type

178
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:22,860
is better than you.

179
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,210
Deceiving a young girl's feelings

180
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:25,180
to get information.

181
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:27,060
Where's your conscience, Commander Ning?

182
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:27,980
Conscience?

183
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:28,620
My lady.

184
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:29,740
Did you think about morality

185
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:31,400
when you threw the knife at me?

186
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:49,730
Song Yiqiu.

187
00:08:49,970 --> 00:08:50,610
You owe me!

188
00:08:50,730 --> 00:08:52,940
You've lived in my house
for over 20 years,

189
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:54,420
and I fed you well.

190
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,500
Have you ever paid rent?

191
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,530
20 years?

192
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:57,940
In these 20 years,

193
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:59,180
the treasures of mine you broke

194
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,660
could buy 20 of your crappy houses.

195
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:01,730
Crappy house?

196
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,330
Then move out!

197
00:09:03,330 --> 00:09:05,540
After all, we both lived just fine

198
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:06,660
for those 72 years without each other.

199
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:07,570
72 years?

200
00:09:07,570 --> 00:09:09,330
It's 72 years and 37 days.

201
00:09:09,330 --> 00:09:10,450
You have such a good memory.

202
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:11,940
Do you need me to praise you?

203
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,180
Move out.

204
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:15,610
I want you to move out right now!

205
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:16,300
Fine.

206
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,330
You know what?

207
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:18,660
Property prices have dropped.

208
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,690
I'll go buy a bigger house than yours.

209
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:21,780
Ning Changyue.

210
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:23,570
Move out.

211
00:09:23,570 --> 00:09:24,420
Breaking news.

212
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:26,610
A man has reportedly been turned
into an osmanthus sapling

213
00:09:26,610 --> 00:09:28,490
and buried in Chengxi Park.

214
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,180
According to witnesses,

215
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:32,690
there was another
young woman at the scene.

216
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:35,110
She is believed to be around 18 years old.

217
00:09:35,110 --> 00:09:36,420
Her identity is unknown,

218
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:40,420
and she is currently being held
at the Chengxi Neighborhood Committee.

219
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:45,300
-Osmanthus tree.
-Osmanthus tree.

220
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:05,910
-Excuse me.
-I'm here to find my child.

221
00:10:07,970 --> 00:10:08,690
What's going on?

222
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,810
Ma'am.

223
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:14,330
We lost our child.

224
00:10:14,330 --> 00:10:15,730
Calm down, calm down.

225
00:10:15,730 --> 00:10:17,660
Take your time, I'll register it.

226
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:19,460
Come, let's get you registered.

227
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,020
Sit down, honey.

228
00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:30,260
Tell me what happened.

229
00:10:30,590 --> 00:10:31,870
Our child...

230
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:34,260
Our child is lost.

231
00:10:34,690 --> 00:10:35,380
I saw...

232
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:37,210
I saw it on TV.

233
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:38,660
Look at her photo.

234
00:10:38,810 --> 00:10:40,090
She's very pretty.

235
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:40,940
Yes.

236
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:41,540
Look.

237
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:42,850
Let me see.

238
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:44,260
Take a look.

239
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,720
Honey, don't cry.

240
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:52,040
You won't cry once we find her.

241
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,690
You look so pretty even when you cry.

242
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:54,260
Come.

243
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,140
Have some tea.

244
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:56,090
No.

245
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:57,380
I want my girl.

246
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:58,490
I want my girl.

247
00:10:58,490 --> 00:11:00,900
Say something.

248
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:02,300
Okay, okay.

249
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:03,300
My wife hasn't

250
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,540
slept well for days.

251
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:05,180
Sorry to bother you.

252
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,840
We'll take our child home now.

253
00:11:08,330 --> 00:11:09,660
Yours?

254
00:11:10,690 --> 00:11:12,050
Biological?

255
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:15,940
That's not right.

256
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,540
You two are just in your early thirties.

257
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:21,430
And this girl is already 18.

258
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,180
We got married early.

259
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,850
And we take good care of ourselves.

260
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,050
Did you bring your household register?

261
00:11:33,250 --> 00:11:34,650
I don't know the process.

262
00:11:37,490 --> 00:11:38,570
I knew it.

263
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,060
There's something wrong with you two.

264
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:42,020
I'm calling the...

265
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:43,180
Time, freeze!

266
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:07,810
Princess and Guard.

267
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:10,210
Are you here to take me home?

268
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:36,870
Back in the Southern Qin,

269
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:39,580
your hand was chained to that iron chain.

270
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:42,020
That was when you gave us the elixir.

271
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:49,490
Eat it.

272
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:55,140
Maybe you can get a chance
to be together forever.

273
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:09,310
You forgot everything?

274
00:13:11,570 --> 00:13:13,120
What's wrong with the princess?

275
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,380
Is there something wrong with her brain?

276
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,420
I've asked everything

277
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,340
you wanted to ask.

278
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,320
What she remembers

279
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,980
depends entirely on her mood.

280
00:13:21,490 --> 00:13:22,420
It's choking me.

281
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:23,490
Watch closely.

282
00:13:23,490 --> 00:13:26,000
Nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium
in a 1:1:1 ratio.

283
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,060
Don't move around,

284
00:13:27,690 --> 00:13:29,420
or it won't be absorbed evenly.

285
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:36,660
Your skills are much better than
in the Republic of China era.

286
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,510
You still remember.

287
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:39,730
Thank you.

288
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,620
You make a fuss every few decades.

289
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,810
This time you even got on TV.

290
00:13:42,810 --> 00:13:44,540
How am I the one making a fuss?

291
00:13:44,850 --> 00:13:46,540
He provoked me.

292
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:50,690
Why are you littering?

293
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:53,780
Pick up this trash by the tree right now.

294
00:13:53,850 --> 00:13:55,060
I'll only say it once.

295
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:58,540
Apologize to them.

296
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,280
Are sanitation workers nowadays

297
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,670
all this good-looking?

298
00:14:04,690 --> 00:14:06,770
You've used up your chance.

299
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,980
She gave us eternal life,

300
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:37,290
but she completely
forgot about it herself.

301
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,450
She's much better than
in the Republic of China era.

302
00:14:39,450 --> 00:14:41,380
Now she even knows how to talk back.

303
00:14:44,850 --> 00:14:46,730
So you're telling me

304
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:49,250
I'm supposed to keep taking care of her,

305
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,850
wait until she
gets her memories back someday,

306
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:54,780
and then ask her
how to end this immortality?

307
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:59,540
Have you seen what you two have done

308
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,470
to my garden?

309
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,580
You've trashed this beautiful garden,

310
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,980
and you expect me
to keep taking care of her?

311
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:19,420
Anyway, until we put an end
to this immortality for good,

312
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,810
I think the three of us
should live together.

313
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:23,020
What three?

314
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:24,520
It's just me.

315
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:27,780
Did you forget you were
just kicked out yesterday?

316
00:15:28,230 --> 00:15:29,030
Come on.

317
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:34,130
Think about it carefully.

318
00:15:34,130 --> 00:15:36,320
This is our only clue in 26 years.

319
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:39,570
This clue is now planted
in that flowerpot.

320
00:15:54,330 --> 00:15:56,300
Then clean all this up.

321
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:58,300
It's all piled up in a mess.

322
00:15:58,330 --> 00:15:59,930
If I catch you doing it again,

323
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,060
you'll live in the garden too.

324
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:10,660
Why does the princess
seem like a different person?

325
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:12,620
She's not quite the same as before.

326
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:14,400
Why did I also hear

327
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:17,240
that you are looking for
a way to end eternal life?

328
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,180
Yes.

329
00:16:19,690 --> 00:16:20,330
Why?

330
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,350
Didn't you want to live before?

331
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:26,850
Maybe we forgot

332
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:29,520
why we wanted to live.

333
00:16:31,210 --> 00:16:32,210
I'm done talking.

334
00:16:39,490 --> 00:16:41,090
What did you drop?

335
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:44,640
This.

336
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,080
It has an ancient smell.

337
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:57,970
What did you feel?

338
00:17:08,950 --> 00:17:10,230
I'm thirsty.

339
00:17:10,250 --> 00:17:10,800
Okay.

340
00:17:10,829 --> 00:17:11,589
Coming.

341
00:17:15,619 --> 00:17:16,690
That painting just now,

342
00:17:16,690 --> 00:17:18,150
Autumn Moon in the Forest,

343
00:17:18,170 --> 00:17:20,490
seems to be a sacred painting
of the Osmanthus Clan.

344
00:17:20,490 --> 00:17:21,250
Could it be connected to

345
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:22,970
our Live Forever Contract?

346
00:17:24,450 --> 00:17:25,730
Next up

347
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:27,349
[Yide Auction Co., Ltd.]

348
00:17:26,490 --> 00:17:28,099
is Autumn Moon in the Forest.

349
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:32,530
The artist and exact date

350
00:17:32,530 --> 00:17:33,890
of this painting are unknown.

351
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:35,450
However, experts have determined that

352
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:37,970
it dates back at least two thousand years.

353
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:41,770
Its depiction of mountains and rivers,
along with its distinctive brushwork,

354
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:43,490
is exceptionally rare for its time.

355
00:17:43,490 --> 00:17:45,960
It is also being shown
to the public for the first time.

356
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:47,850
At the collector's request,

357
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:50,650
the painting cannot
be fully unveiled at this time.

358
00:17:50,650 --> 00:17:52,210
We appreciate your understanding.

359
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:54,010
The opening bid is 800,000 yuan.

360
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,510
Bidding starts now.

361
00:17:59,940 --> 00:18:02,050
A piece by an unknown artist

362
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:03,620
with no known provenance,

363
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:05,680
yet they dare to sell it half-hidden.

364
00:18:05,850 --> 00:18:07,160
Who would buy it?

365
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:07,860
Uncle,

366
00:18:08,210 --> 00:18:10,490
are we going to bid on this painting?

367
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,210
I don't think it's worth that much.

368
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,250
Let them bid.

369
00:18:14,250 --> 00:18:15,210
I'm not bidding.

370
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:17,370
This painting is actually quite good.

371
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:21,340
It contains the time
of those bound by the pact.

372
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:22,900
As long as you get it

373
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:25,200
and release your time from the painting,

374
00:18:25,210 --> 00:18:26,870
you can end your immortality.

375
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:30,660
But are you sure you want to do this?

376
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:34,050
Let's go.

377
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:36,880
Are we really just leaving like this?

378
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:18,970
Mr. 250, one million, going once.
